    "questionText": "A subject is studied at the exact moment of maximal inspiration, when the lungs and chest wall are at their greatest expansion and no air is flowing at the mouth. Simultaneous measurements record an alveolar pressure of 0 cm H2O and an intrapleural pressure of -8 cm H2O. What is the transmural pressure across the alveolar wall at this instant, and in which direction does it act?",
